course: dictionary
lesson: 1388
title: Captive: kept and not free
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A captive is a person or animal that has been caught and is kept somewhere, and is not allowed to leave. Captive can also be an adjective, which describes something that is kept and not free, like captive animals.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Daniel and his friends, captives in Babylon, kept God's food laws.» Daniel was not free to go home, so captives must be people who are kept somewhere against their will.
explain: Try swapping in your meaning. «Mediterranean galleys were often rowed by prisoners, captives and enslaved people.» Prisoners, captives and enslaved people are all kept and not free, so the meaning fits.
explain: Captive is also used with «taken» and «held». «The soldiers took the people captive» means they caught them and kept them. A captive audience must listen because they cannot leave.
fact: A captive is a noun for a person or animal that has been caught and kept.
fact: Captive is an adjective when it describes something kept and not free, such as «captive animals».
fact: «Taken captive» and «held captive» both mean caught and kept, and not allowed to leave.
fact: In science, captive breeding means animals are bred while they are kept by people, as in zoos.
fact: «Roksolana, a captive, became the wife of Sultan Suleiman the Magnificent.» Even as a captive, she became very powerful at court, but she did not rule the empire.
exercise: «The soldiers took the people captive and kept them in the town.» What does taken captive mean? | Left alone to rest | Given a gift and sent home | *Caught and kept, not free | Asked to sing a song
exercise: «Captive animals» are kept in one place. What does captive mean here? | Very fast | *Kept and not free | Wild and happy | Asleep
exercise: «A captive audience must listen because they cannot leave.» Why must they listen? | *They cannot leave | They are deaf | They want to sing | They are very tired
test: «Roksolana, a captive from Rohatyn, became the wife of a sultan.» Which meaning of captive fits here? | *A captive is a person caught and kept, not free | A captive is a king who rules a land | A captive is a fast horse | A captive is a happy singer
test: «The people were held captive in Babylon for many years.» What does held captive mean? | Invited to a great feast | *Kept somewhere and not allowed to leave | Trained to become soldiers | Given a new home by choice
exam: «Captive animals in a zoo are kept and not free.» What does captive mean in this sentence? | *Kept and not free | Loud and noisy | Very hungry | Wild and free
